WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.906
Objections are information, not insults.

00:00:01.906 --> 00:00:04.575
This lesson is about objection map basics.

00:00:04.575 --> 00:00:05.718
Objections are information.

00:00:05.718 --> 00:00:08.387
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:08.387 --> 00:00:12.199
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:12.199 --> 00:00:17.917
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:22.111
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:22.111 --> 00:00:26.304
Stay practical: map four objections before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:26.624 --> 00:00:30.602
Map four objections you expect: money, time, trust, and timing.

00:00:30.602 --> 00:00:32.989
Remember the objective: map four objections.

00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:37.365
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:37.365 --> 00:00:42.139
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:42.139 --> 00:00:46.514
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:46.514 --> 00:00:51.288
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:51.288 --> 00:00:54.073
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:54.073 --> 00:00:55.664
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:55.984 --> 00:00:59.785
For each, write a calm reply and a clarifying question.

00:00:59.785 --> 00:01:02.065
Remember the objective: map four objections.

00:01:02.065 --> 00:01:06.245
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

